    "why": "THE SPLIT-AT-MIDNIGHT READING, AND THE ONE CASE THAT INVERTS UNDER THE ANCHOR-DATE ONE. p-ali holds a single 20:00-08:00 night on the 2nd, which is four hours on the 2nd and eight on the 3rd. Against a cap of six hours in one day the 3rd is over and the 2nd is not — and under the anchor-date reading every neighbouring type uses, the whole twelve hours would land on the 2nd and the two answers would swap. p-noor holds a 08:00-20:00 day duty that crosses no midnight, so its hours stay on their own date, which is what stops the case being read as \"this type ignores the anchor date\".",
